WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.050
Let’s put numbers on doubling the angle.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.150
Follow the diagram.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.450
You’re running at ten knots.

4
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.525
At ten twelve, a light is thirty degrees on the bow.

5
00:00:11.775 --> 00:00:14.975
At ten thirty, it’s sixty degrees on the bow.

6
00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:17.175
The angle has doubled.

7
00:00:17.425 --> 00:00:19.350
How far did you run?

8
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.850
Eighteen minutes at ten knots.

9
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.475
Three miles.

10
00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:28.000
So at ten thirty you were three miles from the light.

11
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.200
And that gives you a fix.

12
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.975
You have a bearing at ten thirty, and you have a distance.

13
00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:40.225
Measure three miles from the light, back along the reciprocal of the bearing, and mark your position.

14
00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:42.275
That’s lesson eight.

15
00:00:42.525 --> 00:00:45.550
Advance the first line by the distance run.

16
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.400
Bow and beam: distance run equals distance off.

17
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.650
Double the angle, and the same thing holds.

18
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.975
Next time: current.
